{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c4855f68-0c8c-40e8-9726-90203abb0d47","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have resolved the cache eviction issue and documented the solution in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-Hx7r6k/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n- **Root Cause**: In [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-Hx7r6k/bot.py), `build_system()` concatenated the static coaching instructions and dynamic athlete context into a single system prompt block with `cache_control`. Any call to `save_fact` appended memory to the athlete profile, modifying this single block and causing Claude's prefix cache to invalidate the instructions.\n- **Fix**: Separated `build_system()` into two distinct system prompt blocks:\n  1. A static prefix block containing `INSTRUCTIONS` with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`.\n  2. A dynamic block containing `athlete_context(a, today)`.\n- Updates to athlete memory via `save_fact` no longer mutate the cached instructions prefix, preserving cache hits across subsequent calls.\n","duration_seconds":46.959895,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":86377,"output_tokens":1355,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":207839,"total_tokens":87732}}}
